hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"262","Jāa a'rābīyun ilá rasūlillāhi ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam fa qāla: 'allimnī kalāman aqūluhu. Qāla: Qul (Lā ilāha illallāhu waḥdahu lā sharīka lah, Allāhu akbaru kabīra, wal-ḥamdu lillāhi kathīra, subḥānallāhi rabbil-'ālamīn, lā ḥawla wa lā quwwata illā billāhil-'azīzil-ḥakīm). Qāla: Fa hāulā'i li-rabbī, fa mā lī? Qāla: Qul (Allāhumma ighfir lī, warḥamnī, wahdinī, warzuqnī).. A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: \"Teach me some words that I may say.\" He (the Prophet) said: \"Say: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; Allah is the Greatest, very great; praise be to Allah, abundantly; glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; there is no power and no strength except with Allah, the Almighty, the Wise.'\" The Bedouin said: \"These are for my Lord, so what is for me?\" He (the Prophet) said: \"Say: 'O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, and provide for me.'\""
"263","Allāhummaghfir lī, warḥamnī, waḥdinī, wa `āfinī warzuqnī. Whenever anyone accepted Islam, the Prophet (ﷺ) used to teach him how to pray then he would instruct him to invoke Allah with the following words: O Allah forgive me, and have mercy on me and guide me and give me good health and provide for me. Reference: Muslim 4/2073, and in one of Muslim's reports there is the addition: 'For these words combine [the goodness of] this world and the next.'"
"264","Alḥamdulillāh and the most excellent words of remembrance are: Lā ilāha illallāh. The most excellent invocation is: Praise is for Allah. and the most excellent words of remembrance are: There is none worthy of worship but Allah. Reference: At-Tirmidhi 5/462, Ibn Majah 2/1249, and Al-Hakim who graded it authentic and Ath-Tbahabi agreed 1/503. See Al-Albani, Sahihul-Jami' As-Saghir 1/362."
"265","Al-Baqiyat al-Salihat: (Subhan Allah), (wa Alhamdulillah), (wa La ilaha illallah), (wa Allahu Akbar), (wa La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah).. The everlasting righteous deeds: \"Glory be to Allah,\" \"Praise be to Allah,\" \"There is no god but Allah,\" \"Allah is the Greatest,\" and \"There is no power and no strength except with Allah.\""
"266","'An 'Abdillah bin 'Amr, radiallahu 'anhuma, qala: Ra'aytu an-nabiyya, sallallahu 'alayhi wa-salam, ya'qidu at-tasbih bi-yamini-hi.. On the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: \"I saw the Prophet (peace be upon him) counting his tasbih (glorification) with his right hand.\""
"267","Idhā kāna junḥu al-layli — aw amsaytum — fa-kuffū ṣibyānakum, fa-inna al-shayāṭīna tantashiru ḥīna'idh, fa-idhā dhāhā sāʿatun min al-layli fa-khallūhum, wa-aghliqū al-abwāba wa-udhkurū isma Allāh; fa-inna al-shayṭānā lā yaftaḥu bāban mughlaqan, wa-awkū qirabakum, wa-udhkurū isma Allāh, wa-khammirū āniyatakum, wa-udhkurū isma Allāh, wa-law an taʿrḍū ʿalayhā shay'an, wa-aṭfi'ū maṣābīḥakum.. When the darkness of night falls — or when you reach the evening — restrain your children, for the devils spread out at that time. After an hour of the night has passed, let them go, and close the doors and mention the name of Allah, for the devil does not open a closed door. Tie up your water-skins and mention the name of Allah, cover your vessels and mention the name of Allah — even if you place something over them — and extinguish your lamps."
